{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AqY5DLmyJuneW7focY8zGG","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t      - R2.6:\n101\t          text: |\n102\t            Must set LC_ALL=C in the environment for both binaries unless the DiffTest.Env\n103\t            explicitly overrides LC_ALL. This ensures deterministic sort order and formatting\n104\t            across locales. The harness applies this default before merging DiffTest.Env.\n105\t\n106\t  R3:\n107\t    title: Comparison and reporting\n108\t    items:\n109\t      - R3.1:\n110\t          text: Must apply the DiffTest.Normalize function (if non-nil) to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison.\n111\t      - R3.2:\n112\t          text: Must compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n113\t      - R3.3:\n114\t          text: Must compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n115\t      - R3.4:\n116\t          text: Must compare exit codes exactly. A difference must be reported as a test failure.\n117\t      - R3.5:\n118\t          text: 'Must report divergence with the following information in the failure message: the DiffTest args, the stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference stderr, the Go stderr, and both exit codes.'\n119\t      - R3.6:\n120\t          text: Must run each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run) so individual test case failures are identifiable in go test output.\n121\t\n122\t  R4:\n123\t    title: Normalization hooks\n124\t    items:\n125\t      - R4.1:\n126\t          text: Must allow per-DiffTest normalization via the Normalize field. The function receives the raw output bytes and returns the normalized bytes.\n127\t      - R4.2:\n128\t          text: Must provide a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string. This normalizer is used by cmd/ts tests.\n129\t      - R4.3:\n130\t          text: |\n131\t            Must allow normalizers to be composed: the harness must accept a slice of Normalize\n132\t            functions applied in order, not a single function. When the slice is nil or empty,\n133\t            no normalization is applied.\n134\t      - R4.4:\n135\t          text: |\n136\t            Must provide func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that returns\n137\t            a single NormalizeFunc applying the given functions in order. This is a convenience\n138\t            for cmd/ test files that combine multiple normalizers:\n139\t\n140\t              normalize := testutils.ComposeNormalizers(\n141\t                  testutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n142\t                  customNormalizer,\n143\t              )\n144\t\n145\t  R5:\n146\t    title: File-state comparison\n147\t    items:\n148\t      - R5.1:\n149\t          text: |\n150\t            Must support utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge,\n151\t            cp, mv). DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is a map[string][]byte where keys are file paths\n152\t            relative to the working directory and values are the expected byte content after\n153\t            execution. When ExpectedFiles is non-nil, the harness checks each entry after both\n154\t            binaries complete.\n155\t      - R5.2:\n156\t          text: |\n157\t            Must compare each ExpectedFiles entry byte-for-byte against the file produced by\n158\t            the Go binary. Any difference must be reported as a test failure with the same\n159\t            format as stdout divergence: file path, expected content (from reference), actual\n160\t            content (from Go binary). Missing files must also be reported as failures.\n161\t\n162\tnon_goals:\n163\t  - pkg/testutils does not build or compile the Go binaries under test.\n164\t  - pkg/testutils does not install or manage Homebrew reference binaries.\n165\t  - pkg/testutils does not produce test reports beyond standard go test output.\n166\t  - pkg/testutils does not implement retry logic; a failing test fails immediately.\n167\t  - pkg/testutils does not mock or stub the filesystem or OS for unit testing cmd/ packages.\n168\t\n169\tpackage_contract:\n170\t  exports:\n171\t    - name: DiffTest\n172\t      signature: \"type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\"\n173\t    - name: NormalizeFunc\n174\t      signature: \"type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\"\n175\t    - name: RunDiffTests\n176\t      signature: \"func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\"\n177\t    - name: ComposeNormalizers\n178\t      signature: \"func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\"\n179\t    - name: TimestampNormalizer"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e2149c5-f6e0-4cca-85fb-431cafcf1c4e","uuid":"f6161c53-8014-4fa6-811a-a7b35cdaa2bf","timestamp":"2026-05-13T21:45:45.591Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5067/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml","content":"      - R2.6:\n          text: |\n            Must set LC_ALL=C in the environment for both binaries unless the DiffTest.Env\n            explicitly overrides LC_ALL. This ensures deterministic sort order and formatting\n            across locales. The harness applies this default before merging DiffTest.Env.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Comparison and reporting\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must apply the DiffTest.Normalize function (if non-nil) to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: Must compare exit codes exactly. A difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.5:\n          text: 'Must report divergence with the following information in the failure message: the DiffTest args, the stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference stderr, the Go stderr, and both exit codes.'\n      - R3.6:\n          text: Must run each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run) so individual test case failures are identifiable in go test output.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Normalization hooks\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must allow per-DiffTest normalization via the Normalize field. The function receives the raw output bytes and returns the normalized bytes.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must provide a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string. This normalizer is used by cmd/ts tests.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: |\n            Must allow normalizers to be composed: the harness must accept a slice of Normalize\n            functions applied in order, not a single function. When the slice is nil or empty,\n            no normalization is applied.\n      - R4.4:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that returns\n            a single NormalizeFunc applying the given functions in order. This is a convenience\n            for cmd/ test files that combine multiple normalizers:\n\n              normalize := testutils.ComposeNormalizers(\n                  testutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n                  customNormalizer,\n              )\n\n  R5:\n    title: File-state comparison\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: |\n            Must support utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge,\n            cp, mv). DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is a map[string][]byte where keys are file paths\n            relative to the working directory and values are the expected byte content after\n            execution. When ExpectedFiles is non-nil, the harness checks each entry after both\n            binaries complete.\n      - R5.2:\n          text: |\n            Must compare each ExpectedFiles entry byte-for-byte against the file produced by\n            the Go binary. Any difference must be reported as a test failure with the same\n            format as stdout divergence: file path, expected content (from reference), actual\n            content (from Go binary). Missing files must also be reported as failures.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/testutils does not build or compile the Go binaries under test.\n  - pkg/testutils does not install or manage Homebrew reference binaries.\n  - pkg/testutils does not produce test reports beyond standard go test output.\n  - pkg/testutils does not implement retry logic; a failing test fails immediately.\n  - pkg/testutils does not mock or stub the filesystem or OS for unit testing cmd/ packages.\n\npackage_contract:\n  exports:\n    - name: DiffTest\n      signature: \"type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\"\n    - name: NormalizeFunc\n      signature: \"type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\"\n    - name: RunDiffTests\n      signature: \"func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\"\n    - name: ComposeNormalizers\n      signature: \"func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\"\n    - name: TimestampNormalizer","numLines":80,"startLine":100,"totalLines":288}}}
